// wired limit leaves no room (g_fwire_full), none is tried.
// Several calls at once (DM_NVN_PREWIRE_JOBS, 4 by default; 1: one call after another, as before): the ranges are cut into calls of g_fwire_call bytes, which up to that many
// workers (the calling thread among them) take in order. One thread's calls fault a file page in at a time, each waiting for its read: Ocarina of Time on the iPhone 18 Pro Max
// (132a82bda) paged in 37.6-63.9 MB at 230-350 MB/s at an area load, and the replay and the encode thread waited 150-390 ms for it; the read-ahead (fwire_advise) runs ahead of
// the calls only so far. Disjoint calls wire disjoint map entries (XNU clips at each call's ends and faults with the map unlocked), so they do not wait on each other; each entry
