// The file pages under a range about to be wired, asked for ahead (hle_svc.c dm_guest_file_advise: F_RDADVISE, read into the file cache with nothing mapped, wired or dirtied) when
// res_add_at notes the range, so they are on their way when the commit's mlock calls meet them: the reads go to the disk at once, where the calls' faults read a cluster at a time.
// On a serial queue of its own, with no lock held: res_add_at may hold g_mu and g_res_mu, and nothing that can wait on the disk runs under them (an advice that waits on the APFS lock
// the freeze waited on stalls only this queue). User-initiated, not utility: a utility thread's reads go out as throttled I/O (tier 1), and the commit's page-in, on the replay
// thread, waits for any page whose read is in flight. Advice only: a range the game lets go meanwhile is read in and dropped as any file page. g_fwire_adv: the bytes asked for, for the
// residency line. The weak one: no host (the graphics tests)
