// them). An entry that has sat idle in one of these caches for CV_IDLE_NS is now marked volatile, at a submission's start on the submit thread, and taken back with
// setPurgeableState:NonVolatile when the cache hands it out; one the system emptied meanwhile is dropped and a new one made, as a cache miss would (cv_back). Only caches whose
// entry's content nothing reads again, and only once the GPU is done with it:
//  - render-target heaps waiting for reuse (rh_wait: their texture went after the submissions that used it completed; a reused heap's texture is filled or zeroed anew). The
//    heap is marked as a whole (a placement heap holds one texture at offset 0, and it waits empty);
//  - the upload staging pool's blocks (up_pool_put: from the batch's feedback handler, so the GPU is done; a block is written whole by the next batch before it is read);
//  - same-pass feedback snapshots (fb_cache_t): only between submissions, once their last submission's fence has passed (fb_cache_t fence; a snapshot is valid only in the
