// live texture or buffer. Entries stay in the residency set while volatile: Metal's headers give no rule against it, the background purge keeps its textures in the set too, and
// taking them out and back would cost a residency commit at each reuse; nothing reads a volatile entry, and the one taken back is non-volatile again before any command buffer
