             t ? [NSString stringWithFormat:@" format %lu %lux%lu type %lu usage %#lx", (unsigned long)t.pixelFormat, (unsigned long)t.width, (unsigned long)t.height, (unsigned long)t.textureType, (unsigned long)t.usage].UTF8String : ""); }
}
// A residency commit under way (res_commit: the queued add / remove calls and [g_res commit]): when it began (mach_absolute_time; 0 between commits), its thread, its changes and the
// file pages wired for it. Ocarina of Time froze on the iPhone 18 Pro Max with the replay thread in iokit_user_client_trap under res_commit for 16.5 s holding g_res_commit_mu; the
// freeze detector said so only at its 5 s mark, and the suspend going to the background waited its whole 3 s for the graphics call around it. The detector now names such a commit
// at about 1 s (stall.c), and the suspend stops waiting for it (hle_nvn.c susp_drain): a commit still in the kernel holds g_res, which nothing may touch until it is back. A few
// relaxed stores per commit; mtl_res_commit_stuck reads them without a lock
// ph: 1 while the commit wires its file pages (fwire_all: an mlock pages them in, which can wait on the same APFS lock), 0 in [g_res commit]; one mark for both, so one line.
// While it wires, done counts the bytes its mlock calls have wired and call says when the current call began (fwire_lock), so the line says how far the page-in got and
// whether one call is stuck or the calls go on slowly
// ph 2: a prewire's page-in (DM_NVN_RES_PREWIRE, res_prewire), before its commit takes g_res_commit_mu, in slot [1]; a commit under the lock is in slot [0]. Each slot has one
// writer at a time (the lock's holder; the one prewire), so a commit and a prewire in the kernel together are both seen until each is back
static uint64_t res_kcommit_in(int slot, uint64_t n, uint64_t wired, int ph) {
    rk_mark *m = &g_rk[slot];
    atomic_store_explicit(&m->n, n, memory_order_relaxed); atomic_store_explicit(&m->wired, wired, memory_order_relaxed); atomic_store_explicit(&m->ph, (uint32_t)ph, memory_order_relaxed);
    atomic_store_explicit(&m->done, 0, memory_order_relaxed); atomic_store_explicit(&m->call, 0, memory_order_relaxed);
    atomic_store_explicit(&m->th, pthread_mach_thread_np(pthread_self()), memory_order_relaxed);
    uint64_t at = mach_absolute_time() | 1;
    atomic_store_explicit(&m->at, at, memory_order_release);
    return at;
}
static void res_kcommit_out(int slot, uint64_t at) { uint64_t e = at; atomic_compare_exchange_strong_explicit(&g_rk[slot].at, &e, 0, memory_order_release, memory_order_relaxed); }
// The oldest of the two marks that has been in the kernel min_ns or more: when it began, and what it is into out; 0 with none
uint64_t mtl_res_commit_stuck(uint64_t min_ns, char *out, size_t n) {
    uint64_t now = mach_absolute_time(), at = 0; int k = -1;
    for (int i = 0; i < 2; i++) { uint64_t a = atomic_load_explicit(&g_rk[i].at, memory_order_acquire); if (a && (!at || a < at)) { at = a; k = i; } }
    if (k < 0) return 0;
    double s = now > at ? mach_s(now - at) : 0;   // the mark is its tick | 1, so a look in the same tick can read one under it
    if (s * 1e9 < (double)min_ns) return 0;
    if (out && n) {
        rk_mark *m = &g_rk[k];
        unsigned long long ch = (unsigned long long)atomic_load_explicit(&m->n, memory_order_relaxed); double mb = atomic_load_explicit(&m->wired, memory_order_relaxed) / 1048576.0;
        uint32_t th = atomic_load_explicit(&m->th, memory_order_relaxed), ph = atomic_load_explicit(&m->ph, memory_order_relaxed);
        if (ph) {
            uint64_t call = atomic_load_explicit(&m->call, memory_order_relaxed); char cur[48] = "between two calls";
            if (call) snprintf(cur, sizeof cur, "the current call %.1f s in", now > call ? mach_s(now - call) : 0);
            snprintf(out, n, "a residency commit's page-in (mlock of %.0f MB of file pages before [g_res commit], %llu changes; %.0f MB wired so far in calls of %.0f MB, %s) in the kernel "
                     "for %.1f s on host thread %#x, %s", mb, ch, atomic_load_explicit(&m->done, memory_order_relaxed) / 1048576.0,
                     g_fwire_call / 1048576.0, cur, s, th, ph == 2 ? "before its commit takes the residency commit lock (DM_NVN_RES_PREWIRE)" : "holding the residency commit lock");
        } else snprintf(out, n, "a residency commit ([g_res commit], %llu changes, %.0f MB of file pages wired for it) in the kernel for %.1f s on host thread %#x, holding the residency commit lock", ch, mb, s, th);
    }
    return at;
}
// A residency commit of g_slow_commit_ns or more (the queued add / remove calls and [g_res commit] together): its line, with what it applied (each change still holds its allocation)
// The sizes are summed while each change still holds its allocation (res_commit_sizes, under g_res_commit_mu, before the release), and the line is written after the unlock
typedef struct { uint64_t na, nr, ba, br; } res_sizes;
static void res_commit_sizes(const res_op *q, size_t n, res_sizes *z) {
    *z = (res_sizes){0};
    for (size_t i = 0; i < n; i++) { uint64_t b = ((__bridge id<MTLAllocation>)q[i].o).allocatedSize; if (q[i].add) { z->na++; z->ba += b; } else { z->nr++; z->br += b; } }
}
static void res_commit_slow(const res_sizes *z, uint64_t dt) {
    static _Atomic uint64_t nslow; uint64_t k = slow_due(&nslow); if (!k) return;
    uint64_t na = z->na, nr = z->nr, ba = z->ba, br = z->br;
    char th[64]; slow_thread(th, sizeof th);
    MLOG("[RED] slow residency commit: %.1f ms (adds %llu, %.1f MB; removes %llu, %.1f MB) on thread %s%s (#%llu)", dt / 1e6, (unsigned long long)na, ba / 1048576.0,
         (unsigned long long)nr, br / 1048576.0, th, on_feedback_q() ? ", on the feedback queue" : t_rca_role == 1 ? ", on the commit worker for the replay (DM_NVN_RES_ASYNC)" :
         t_rca_role == 2 ? ", before a queue commit (DM_NVN_RES_ASYNC)" : "", (unsigned long long)k);
}
// ---------- The page-in outside the residency commit lock (DM_NVN_RES_PREWIRE) ----------
// Ocarina of Time on the iPhone 18 Pro Max (a464a49e6, NX18-X2.0 traces/oot-mst-1-findings.md): "slow residency commit: 174.3 ms (adds 374, 201.7 MB)" on the commit worker, and the
// encode thread and the replay waited 178.0 and 176.9 ms for g_res_commit_mu behind it; the 300 frames around it spent 271.7 of the worker's 340.0 ms of commits in the mlock page-in
// of guest-file pages (upload sources, line 6254: the guest's texture data, paged out under memory pressure), not in [g_res commit]. While a commit held the lock through that page-in,
// every queue commit (the encode thread's, a present snapshot's, a one-off's) and every other commit waited for it, whether or not it needed what was being paged in.
// Now the page-in runs before the lock (res_prewire): a commit first wires the file ranges of the changes it must apply, in chunks of up to g_pw_chunk bytes, with g_res_commit_mu
// free, then takes the lock only for the add / remove calls and [g_res commit] of the changes below the chunk's end (res_commit_take), and goes on with the next chunk. The rule
// stays: a commit that returns has every change it was asked for in the set. A commit that needs a change whose range another thread is wiring waits for that prewire
// (g_pw_cv; its own line when slow), then commits it itself or finds it committed; one that needs none of them (the encode thread's queue commits of command buffers recorded before
// those changes, rca_queue_guard: the number the replay gave the record; a queue commit itself, which needs only the lock) goes through at once. One prewire runs at a time.
// =0 wires under the lock again and takes the whole queue, as before (res_commit_all); =ab alternates with DM_AB. The residency line counts the prewires, their waits and the guards
// that found their changes committed
static size_t g_pw_chunk = 64u << 20;   // bytes of file ranges a prewire wires before its commit (t_res_prewire makes it smaller)
static uint64_t g_rpw_n, g_rpw_bytes, g_rpw_ns, g_rpw_waits, g_rpw_wait_ns, g_rpw_wait_max;   // prewires, the bytes and time they wired; waits for one, their time, the longest (under g_res_mu)
static _Atomic uint64_t g_rg_n, g_rg_skip;   // the encode thread's queue-commit guards, and those that found every change they needed committed (rca_queue_guard)
static int g_pw_mode = -1;
static int pw_on(void) {
