// dead, so a pass asks first the member that kept it at the last pass (NvImageHeap's hint), then its most recently used member (the largest last use); if either is not dead the family
// stays and no other member is asked. Only when both are dead are the rest asked, and the old rule decides as it did: the family goes only whole, when every member the table holds is
