    rmu_lock();
    treg_drop_pool_views(pool);
    smu_lock();
    // The pool's texture IDs are marked gone before their CPU-written classification goes: a pool walk (pool_gpu, holding g_rmu) reaching an ID in between found it not gone, the
    // pool's magic still set and the texture no longer CPU-written, and tex_mtl_ handed out its packaged entry (an NvPkg) as the texture: "-[NvPkg buffer]: unrecognized selector"
    // in tex_by_id (Ocarina of Time, see reference/nvn-objects.md). Marked first, a reader holding g_rmu is done before, or finds the ID gone and takes tex_made. The classification
    // goes before the Finalize is counted: a reading at or past the count finds none of the pool's records to hand over (cpu_unc_drop). g_smu → g_cpu_tex_mu, as mtl_tex_release
    cpu_tex_drop_pool(pool);
