// Host CPU reads of a texture's whole storage (ported from S2Arm 90bda409, 5eb20239, f94ab7f1, 19710ac2, e41390d4, Apache-2.0). A game maps only the part of a texture's declared
// storage it uses: the rest can be a reserved range with no access, and storage outside every registered pool can have pages whose protection reads but whose backing is gone (a
// file truncated under a shared mapping). A whole read of such storage stopped the host with SIGBUS in pkg_upload's CPU deswizzle. mem_readable: the bytes from p on, up to n, that
// the VM regions there let the CPU read (vm_region_64 region by region: mach_vm.h is not in the iOS SDK); safe_copy: n bytes copied page by page with vm_read_overwrite, which returns
// an error for a page it cannot read instead of faulting, unreadable pages as 0, and the bytes read
static uint64_t mem_readable(const void *p, uint64_t n) {
