// Partial re-upload (DM_NVN_REUPLOAD_PART=0 turns it off): a re-upload deswizzles only the levels and layers whose storage was written since the content it builds on was read, and keeps
// the others: in the spare it is made into (the content as of the spare's own upload), or copied on the GPU from the texture it replaces (as of the last upload), in the upload batch.
// Written: a CPU write into its pages (the page tracking; a page shared by two levels or layers counts as written for both), or a GPU store into the storage since (gsb_log_since: a copy
// or clear into this texture or into another texture object over the same storage, or a render pass that drew into one, gsb_store). A re-upload into the spare after a store through this
// texture's own record is whole (tex_mtl_: the spare was read before it). Only for the staged GPU deswizzle of a texture neither the game nor the host draws into or writes as an image
// (no render-target or shader-write usage, not the direct path). NieR:Automata writes 28x28 to 244x244 regions into layers 0 and 1 of two 16-layer arrays every frame in its heavy scenes
// (WriteTexels), 48 MB re-uploaded whole a frame where 6 MB had changed
