// Coalesced re-uploads (DM_NVN_REUPLOAD_COALESCE=0 turns both halves off, as before). Ocarina of Time re-uploaded a whole single-level atlas several times a frame for a few written pages
// (11 times in one frame; 176 MB staged for a 5% written share; NX18-X2.0 oot-alldata-analysis.md, fix 4):
// - Banded: a re-upload of an image (a layer's level, not 3D) written in part deswizzles only its block-row bands (8 << the level's block height rows of blocks, contiguous in the storage)
//   whose bytes were written since the content it builds on was read, and keeps the other bands: as the spare it goes into holds them, or copied from the texture it replaces (a region
//   copy beside the bands' copies; none overlap, so the batch's one encoder needs no order among them). A written image whose bands are all clean (only its padding was written) is kept.
// - Deferred: a texture's pages written since its upload are re-uploaded at a use only if the submission being encoded needs them. The game's writes made before it submitted the commands
