// and depth entry (g_depth_zero when it loaded); a failed preparation hands nil to those that joined it and leaves the table, so the next caller tries again. The owner holds
// the record's latch (an unfair lock) across its load, so a draw that joins a utility-QoS prefetch lends it its priority; the table lock is never held across a load or a wait.
// A load that is only queued (a prefetch block not yet run) has no record: a draw that comes first loads the library itself and the queued block takes its result.
