static int tidle_older(const void *a, const void *b) { uint32_t x = ((const tidle_cand *)a)->used, y = ((const tidle_cand *)b)->used; return x < y ? -1 : x > y; }
// The footprint cap's back-off: a sweep for the cap that frees under TIDLE_FOOT_LITTLE (the footprint is mostly what the sweep cannot take) doubles the time to the next one, up to
// TIDLE_FOOT_MAX_NS, instead of walking every serial entry under g_rmu / g_smu each second on the submit thread; the footprint under the cap or a sweep that frees that much sets it
// back to a second. Said once. The headroom's sweeps (DM_NVN_IDLE_TEX_MB) keep their second
