// serializes a period's archive, and a compile under way through another compiler then reads one: SIGSEGV in MultiLevelAirntBinaryCache::getElementAtDestination under
// newRenderPipelineStateWithDescriptor, every time with the MTLBinaryArchive_Serialize thread in airntSerializeToURL (upstream: Super Mario Party's prebuild of 39,111 pairs, three
// crashes on an M4 Pro with macOS 27.2, after 4,000 to 22,000 pairs). The cause is in Metal: the host keeps the two apart. A serialization waits for the compiles under way and
// holds new ones back until it is written (writer first: the prebuild's workers would otherwise keep it waiting for good); every compile of the archive's paths (arch_capture_try,
// arch_capture_cs: the capture and the plain compiles beside it) goes through here. NX 18's own guard of two captures of one shader function (fn_claim) is taken before this one
static pthread_mutex_t g_ser_mu = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
