// DM_NVN_ARGS_PARTIAL: whether sh's block can be copied with only some kinds' entries written again, and which (PK_*; 0 no; tm / sm: the texture and sampler slots that moved, bit slot % 64).
// The block must be one a reuse would take but for those changes: of this pass with no new pass or program since (as the pass rule's ab_gen, without the hard changes), or one the
// cross-pass rule keeps (args_xpass_ok without its hard generation: this submission, a block for the pass's own encoder, its sample count, no write since a block of copies), with its
// pool and handle tables current. Each hard change since it must be in the stage's history (g_args_pk: a texture, sampler or storage binding; any other raised the floor past ab_pkh).
// A base instance change (shaders reading c0) and a uniform change (any shader on the list: the uniform patch's kinds) are patched with them. Only the vertex and fragment stages,
// with kinds on args_pkind's list (no handles or addresses read from memory, no raw pool table, no geometry emulation buffers), and not under the resource check or the pass dump
static int args_partial(NvShader *sh, int st, int xpass, int pool, uint64_t *tm, uint64_t *sm) {
