// The plan's stage 2 gives want-listed fragment shaders a second path: their sampled textures and samplers read from a slot table of resource IDs indexed by NVN slot, built only
// when a binding changes, as copy-on-change arena blocks, so a texture rebind becomes a pointer patch. Stage 1 builds and checks those tables on the host beside the slot path, and
// counts what they would save; no shader or pipeline changes. One table for the fragment stage: textures by slot (combined and separate: tex_slot_h's reg), samplers by slot
// (SAMP reg, SAMPT 128 + reg). An entry holds what the slot path wrote for it (tex_resolve / samp_resolve, the one resolver), with the handle and the declared type and class it was
// resolved for. Converted kinds (bl_conv): a sampled 2D, 2D array, cube, cube array or 3D texture slot (TEX, no 1D fetch) and a sampler slot without a border twin; handles from
// uniform memory, buffer textures, images, constant samplers, arrays and pools stay slot-bound. Every entry is current while its epoch holds: the registration, guest-write, storage,
// view (g_alt_gen) generations and the submission (the arena block, transient views) unchanged; a move starts a new epoch, and each entry is resolved again at its next use.
// A version is the table as it stands: an entry written moves it (ver), and its arena block is made (copied from the shadow) at the first encode that finds the table moved.
// A shader whose last check saw this version, its stage's texture / sampler binding generation (g_bl_tgen) and epoch takes it without looking at an entry: stage 2's reuse.
// Each encode that resolved texture or sampler slots (in full, or a partial patch) is checked: for each converted binding the slot path's value against the entry, counting the
// resolutions the slot path made against those the table would have needed (entries not current), entries a same-pass feedback snapshot made draw-specific, and mismatches: a
// current entry that differs from the slot path's value, or any entry moved under a version taken without a look, would be a wrong texture in stage 2 (logged, the first 8)
enum { BL_TEX = NTEX, BL_SAMP = 128 + NTEX };
