    // Demand first: this runs after the draw's own pipeline is built. A predicted key whose base is made needs no compile (pso_base_made) and takes nothing here. With hybrid
    // pipelines a predicted draw whose pulling stand-in is ready (made here, from its base made or archived: the work its draw would do) will not wait, and builds its own pipeline
    // on demand (pso_pend_demand). The rest are draws that would wait (a pair whose pulling base is not made yet): at most PSO_PREDICT_BUDGET speculative builds on the global
    // queue, the draws met with their attachments as they are (qa) first, then the guesses with other depth / stencil attachments (qb); every other draw of qa goes to pp_bg_queue
    // (pso_pend_kick_next; upstream PR #1344, with NX 18's queues). DM_NVN_PREDICT_NEXT=0: the budget alone, as before
    // With hybrid pipelines a key whose base is not made has its lookup handed to the background (pso_bg_look, unless DM_NVN_BG_LOOK=0), which admits its build when its draw
    // would wait, by the same rule; the submit thread then makes no stand-in and asks no archive for it. The budget is the prediction's, shared with its workers
    int admitted = 0, next = 0, hy = hybrid_on(), nx = sw_on(predict_next_mode()), bgl = hy && sw_on(bg_look_mode());
    PsoPredictBudget *budget = [PsoPredictBudget new];
